const instructions={"styles":"Recreate [SUBJECT] through the visual language of ELEMENT. Apply the chosen aesthetic as one coherent creative direction across the complete image, allowing its characteristic visual logic to shape the subject without replacing or misidentifying it. Preserve the subject's essential identity and defining structure.","textures":"Apply ELEMENT as the defining tactile and visual texture of [SUBJECT]. Carry the chosen texture coherently across the relevant visible areas so the image reads as one intentional textural treatment. Preserve the subject's identity, silhouette and essential structure.","lighting":"Apply ELEMENT as a complete photographic post-production treatment to the supplied photograph of [SUBJECT]. Treat the source photograph as the fixed image input: preserve the subject, identity, pose, anatomy, scene geometry and original photographic content unless the named process inherently alters tonal or colour information. Recreate the chosen photographic finish through coherent colour grading, tonal response, grain structure, local contrast, retouching and image artefacts appropriate to that treatment. The result must read as a deliberate finished photograph, not a newly generated scene or a lighting setup.","effects":"Apply ELEMENT to [SUBJECT] as one unified visual effect. Make the effect clearly legible, coherent across the image and appropriate to the source, without allowing it to obscure or replace the subject. Preserve essential identity and visual readability.","composition":"Recompose [SUBJECT] using ELEMENT as the governing compositional principle. Make the arrangement feel deliberate and resolved, with a clear visual focus and coherent spatial organisation. Preserve the subject's identity and all explicitly required content.","rendering":"Render [SUBJECT] using ELEMENT as the governing image-creation approach. Apply the method consistently so the complete image feels like one coherent rendering outcome. Preserve the subject's essential identity, structure and intended visual content.","colour-atmosphere":"Reinterpret [SUBJECT] through ELEMENT as one unified colour and atmospheric direction. Carry the chosen visual mood consistently through the image while keeping the subject clear, recognisable and visually coherent."};
