 "Glass & Ceramics":{identity:"an amorphous glass or fired ceramic body; distinguish transparent silicate, opaque body, glaze and crystalline ceramic phases",micro:"resolve wall thickness, glaze pools, kiln texture, bubbles, inclusions, translucency and surface crazing only where the named material allows",process:"show forming, blowing, pressing, slip casting, firing, vitrification, glazing or annealing evidence appropriate to the target",behaviour:"respect brittle fracture, stable wall thickness, thermal shock and the difference between transparent glass and opaque ceramic",optics:"glass uses refraction, Fresnel reflections and transmission; ceramics use body opacity with glaze-specific reflection",limits:"do not turn ceramic into glass, make every ceramic transparent, or add impossible razor-thin glass sections"},
 "Textiles & Fabrics":{identity:"a fibrous assembly whose behaviour depends on fibre chemistry, yarn, weave, knit, pile, felt or laminate construction",micro:"make yarn count, fibre diameter, weave direction, loop structure, pile height and edge finishing visible at a scale appropriate to the source",process:"show spinning, weaving, knitting, felting, braiding, coating or lamination rather than a flat texture pasted over geometry",behaviour:"respect drape, tension, seam placement, fraying, compression and the distinction between woven, knitted and nonwoven materials",optics:"use fibre-level diffuse scatter, directional sheen or pile shadow according to the textile; avoid uniform plastic highlights",limits:"do not convert solid parts into fabric, erase seams or make unsupported cloth spans rigid"},
 "Polymers & Composites":{identity:"a polymer matrix or engineered composite with a defined resin, elastomer, fibre, foam or porous network",micro:"distinguish continuous matrix from reinforcement, fillers, cellular voids, fibres and surface skin",process:"show injection moulding, compression moulding, extrusion, pultrusion, lay-up, curing, foaming or sintering appropriate to the target",behaviour:"respect stiffness, elasticity, creep, fracture, anisotropic reinforcement and the load path of the original component",optics:"match matte, satin, gloss, translucency or fibre reflection to the polymer and reinforcement rather than defaulting to plastic gloss",limits:"do not convert every surface into carbon weave, foam or open lattice; maintain functional wall thickness and joint integrity"},
