for(const entries of Object.values(screenGroups))for(const entry of entries){if(screenVisualOverrides[entry[0]])entry[1]=screenVisualOverrides[entry[0]];}
for(const [subcategory,entries] of Object.entries(screenGroups)) for(const [name,visual] of entries){
 const title=name;
 const prompt=`SOURCE IMAGE / PRIMARY SUBJECT: [SUBJECT] / [SUPPLIED SOURCE IMAGE — THE ORIGINAL PERSON, CHARACTER, ANIMAL OR OBJECT IS THE TRANSFORMATION INPUT]. TARGET SCREEN UNIVERSE: ${name}. Transform the supplied subject as though it has been completely reimagined to belong naturally inside the specific visual universe of ${name}. This is a full subject-and-world transformation, not a surface filter or a simple change of illustration style. Apply the defining visual language of ${name}: ${visual}.

SUBJECT RE-CREATION: Keep the original person, character, animal or object's recognisable core identity and defining features, but redesign its visible presentation so it plausibly belongs in this screen universe. For a person or character, adapt clothing, costume, footwear, accessories, hairstyle or headwear, and any appropriate character styling to the wardrobe, silhouettes, materials and design conventions of ${name}. The subject should look as though they are a character from this world, while remaining recognisably the original source person. Do not merely preserve their original outfit if it conflicts with the target universe. For an object, reinterpret its materials, construction, surface details, proportions and design language so it looks manufactured, used or encountered within this universe. For an animal or creature, adapt its anatomy styling, markings, materials and visual design to the universe while retaining its recognisable identity.

WORLD AND ENVIRONMENT TRANSFORMATION: Rebuild or adapt the surroundings to evoke the specific world of ${name}. Replace incompatible background details with a fitting environment, architecture, interiors, streets, landscapes, technology, set dressing, props, signage shapes and atmospheric elements drawn from the target universe's established visual vocabulary. The location should feel like a believable scene from that show, film, cartoon or anime rather than the unchanged original setting. Use franchise-specific environmental cues and production design, but do not overcrowd the frame or introduce unrelated story events.

UNIFIED ART DIRECTION: Apply the target universe consistently across character design, costume, environment, props, materials, lighting, colour grading, atmosphere, camera language, perspective, linework or rendering technique, and overall production finish. Match the distinctive visual grammar and level of stylisation of ${name}; avoid generic genre shorthand. Make the complete image feel like an authentic frame, key art image or cinematic still from that specific universe.

IDENTITY AND CONTINUITY: Preserve the source subject's recognisable face or defining geometry, core proportions, characteristic expression and essential pose where possible. Allow wardrobe, styling, surface design, background, lighting and composition to change when necessary to achieve a convincing world integration. Do not substitute the subject with an existing named franchise character, and do not add unrelated main characters, logos, watermarks, captions or invented franchise branding. Maintain coherent anatomy, perspective, scale, contact shadows and visual integration.

SCENE CONTROL: [OPTIONAL SCENE / LOCATION / ACTION — IF BLANK, CREATE A NATURAL SCENE THAT FITS THE TARGET UNIVERSE]. The final result must clearly communicate both parts of the transformation: the original subject has been reimagined as someone or something that belongs in ${name}, and the surrounding world has been adapted to match it.`;
 additions.push({id:id++,title,category:"films-shows",desc:`Visual transformation target from Films & Shows / ${subcategory}. Recreate the supplied subject using ${name} visual language.`,prompt,negative:"Do not substitute the source subject with a copyrighted character. No unrelated characters, logos, titles, watermarks, invented props, altered identity, distorted anatomy, inconsistent perspective, generic style dilution or low-resolution artefacts.",kind:"style",bg:"#202832",art:"linear-gradient(135deg,#17233a,#6b477f 55%,#e16a2c)",glow:"#b58be2",model:["Midjourney","DALL·E","Stable Diffusion","Flux"],tags:[subcategory,name,"Visual transformation","Style reference"],difficulty:"Advanced"});
}
